 "about": "Moods and gestures on the stage's generic controls (docs/24-motion.md). Values are in control units: -1 to 1 (0 to 1 for eye_smile and cheek), turned into each character's own parameter values by its calibration. Gestures add to whatever the character is doing; keys are [seconds, value] and each track starts and ends at 0. A gesture is offered for a character only if every control in 'needs' maps to one of its parameters ('a|b': either will do). Arms: arm_left/arm_right turn the whole arm at the shoulder, arm_left_b/arm_right_b the forearm at the elbow; characters made by the studio put a waving arm at 0.5 and 0.85 and a hand on the hip at 0.6 and -0.9 (studio/refine.py).",

